* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# What a site installs is git archive's tarball of a tag (our forge, git.openvibe.codes, and codeload alike): it leaves out
# what only this repository's own checks read (4.284.0; the owner, 11-16: "faster … optimized and efficient"). The tests
# (3.6 MB) and the docs' screenshots (2.9 MB) were two thirds of every site's 10 MB install.
/test/ export-ignore
/docs/screenshots/ export-ignore
/.github/ export-ignore
